    {
      "id": "t010929",
      "source": "Preference rankings; for pair (a,b), sum weights of voters ranking a>b versus b>a.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010930",
      "source": "Part B — New and mixed reasoning domains",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010931",
      "source": "N1. Scale, proportion, and distance",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010932",
      "source": "Problem 626. Map scale 1:10000",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010933",
      "source": "Knowledge context.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010934",
      "source": "Map scale links a model to the real world through proportional reasoning.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010935",
      "source": "Given facts.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010936",
      "source": "A map has scale 1:10000. The measured map distance between two points is 5 cm. Rule: 1 cm on the map represents 10000 cm in reality; 100,000 cm = 1 km.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010937",
      "source": "Rules.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010938",
      "source": "Multiply map length by the scale denominator, then convert units. A scale is a ratio, not an added distance.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010939",
      "source": "Task.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010940",
      "source": "What is the real straight-line distance in kilometres?",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010941",
      "source": "Step-by-step solution.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010942",
      "source": "1. Real centimetres=5×10000=50000. 2. Convert to kilometres: 50000÷100,000=0.5.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010943",
      "source": "Answer.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010944",
      "source": "0.5 km.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010945",
      "source": "Knowledge takeaway.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010946",
      "source": "Scale problems are ratio problems: keep units explicit and conversion becomes mechanical.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010947",
      "source": "Formal model.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t010948",
      "source": "Proportion d_real=d_map×denominator, followed by unit conversion.",
      "translation": ""
    },
