      "id": "t011017",
      "source": "N2. Coordinates and constraint-based location",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011018",
      "source": "Problem 631. Locating a point by constraints: case 1",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011019",
      "source": "Knowledge context.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011020",
      "source": "Coordinates turn location into numbers. Multiple spatial clues can be treated as simultaneous constraints.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011021",
      "source": "Given facts.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011022",
      "source": "A point P lies on an integer grid with x,y from 0 to 7. It satisfies x+y=6 and x−y=0. It also satisfies x≥2.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011023",
      "source": "Rules.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011024",
      "source": "A location is valid only if it satisfies every stated equation and inequality at the same time.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011025",
      "source": "Task.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011026",
      "source": "Which coordinate(s) can P occupy? Is the solution unique?",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011027",
      "source": "Step-by-step solution.",
      "translation": ""
    }
